      "AND THE GRIP WEARS THE CAP\'S LIT LINE, because a part that looks like the cap and is missing the one mark the cap wears reads as a cap with its lamp out. It is the same 2px of `--led-hot` across the waist, and the knurl mask had already cleared the space for it. The job is lighter here than on the plain fader, where that line IS the value: the blade carries the value now and this says the piece is live. Which is also why it is on the grip and never on the blade — orange on the blade would be orange against the orange band, and cutting that band is the blade\'s whole job.",
      "A SHUT BAND KEEPS A LIT SEAM, AND THE VALUES DO NOT MOVE FOR IT. Below three pixels of real span each blade is DRAWN up to a pixel and a half further out and the band is stretched by exactly what the two of them gave up, so the gap holds at 3px however far the ends close — right down to a === b. It is the jaw\u2019s drawn blade that shifts, through `--nudge`; the jaw BOX stays where the value put it, so no hit target ever lies about what it is over. Above three pixels the nudge is zero and the whole mechanism is inert: an end with room to be exact is drawn exactly. What it buys is that a closed span now says something — a hairline of light where the two ends have met, instead of a dark join you have to read the numbers to interpret.",
