      'THE ORBIT BALL CAN BE GLAZED, AND THE GLASS IS SHADED PER PIXEL LIKE EVERYTHING ELSE ON IT. `orbit({ glass: true })` puts a dome over the bore. It went in as CSS first — a stack of radial gradients over the disc — and lasted one look, because the three things that actually identify thick glass are all functions of the NORMAL and a stylesheet has none: the rim goes bright where you look ALONG the wall, the streaks are the room reflected and bent by the curve, and both stay put while the ball turns underneath. That is the same argument that took the arcs off CSS and into the map, arrived at the same way — by drawing a better gradient six times and getting six better gradients.',
