      'THE VIEWPORT PANEL TAKES THE ORBIT BALL. Its flat six-node axis ball was the same control as the six-key pad beneath it — each node snapped to a view, so does each key, and the keys also say which one is current. Two parts for one question, and the one that went is the one that could not answer the other: what if the angle you want is not one of the six. The keys now TURN the ball to their view rather than snapping it, on the same animation the double-click reset uses, because snapping would leave them as two pictures of one state.',
